Correctness/error-contract finding at [input.rs:5](/private/tmp/google-rust-eval-20261023-a/fixtures/05/input.rs:5): unwrap turns expected missing-file, permission, and other read errors into panics. 'Reporting errors' calls for Result when recoverable I/O failures need context. Return the original I/O error so the caller can display it with the path or handle its kind.

```rust
use std::fs;
use std::io;
use std::path::Path;

pub fn load_config(path: &Path) -> Result<String, io::Error> {
    fs::read_to_string(path)
}
```

Callers must handle or propagate the Result. Merely replacing unwrap with expect would retain the incorrect panic policy; catch_unwind is also inappropriate for this expected error. Static review only; this proposal was not compiled.

